ugh the furlough  scheme now the cost of living crisis is  kicking in he's not as popular so this  could be a this is a very big political  test for him but um the real test is  what he does for families who but no  fault of their own are going to find  their electric and gas bills going up to  nearly 2 000 pounds a year a rise of 650  pounds which is too much it's it's  eye-watering and it will put families in  real fuel poverty there'll be families  choosing between feeding themselves and  keeping and whether they can afford to  turn the gas on which is why the chance  has got to come up with something pretty  good tomorrow and suggestions of years  of high gas prices which is part of the  part of the issue especially with the  ukraine russia issue on the back burner  as well but the the other context of  this is uh the leveling up agenda  yorkshire post master plan to radically  improve uk the leveling up papers  pledges on mayors and inequality but  doubts over funding um you know is there  a thumbs up at least um from the  yorkshire post uh for this and what do  you make of what you heard today anna  yeah i mean as you think as you'd expect  because it's the yorkshire post then  there's there is a gentle welcoming of  what michael gove has set out but i i  think there's also within the yorkshire  post and obviously you see it in the eye  i think it is in a number of other  papers you'll you'll see that  the real concern is actually there is no  new money at all so if you've got no  more funding a lot of this is just words  on a piece of paper and and you know do  they admirable aims i mean there is a  there's a fair criticism that you know  we have had 12 years of conservative  government and it's almost an indictment  on the failings of 12 years off that  government but moving on from that i  think the other criticism that we're  seeing coming out of it from some of the  mayors as well in some of the papers is  that actually whilst people like andy  street ove